Catch AI Hallucinations with this new feature! 
 ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌

Hi there, 

Maddie here from Originality.AI 

As you're probably aware, our team has been hard at work developing our
new 

**Fact-Checking Tool,**which is currently in its 

****BETA phase.**** In this email, we're excited to share some insights
into the tool's accuracy based on a study we just completed! 

****Summary of Key Findings: ****

* We compared 6 (six) AI models for fact checking: Originality.ai,
GPT-4, GPT-3.5, CodeLlama-34b, Llama-2-13b, and Llama-2-70b.

* A dataset of 120 recent facts (60 true, 60 false) was created and fed
to each model to test accuracy.

* Originality.ai's Fact Checking tool has the highest accuracy at
72.3%. GPT-4 was second at 64.9%.

* Originality.ai stood out with 0% "unknowns" and low error rate,
indicating reliability.

* When fact checking a generated article, Originality.ai caught more
false facts than GPT-4 and Llama-70b.

Read Full Study Here!

****Why Fact-Checking Matters:****

In a time where the online world is inundated with AI-generated content,
the integrity of information faces a growing challenge posed by LLM
Hallucinations. "Hallucinations" refer to an AI's confident responses
that seemingly lack substantiation from its training data. The
frequency at which hallucinations are  making their way into online
content has been on the rise since the launch of chatGPT. This can lead
to the spread of misinformation and other serious societal risks. 

Here are the hallucination rates for some of the popular LLMs :

**How Originality.ai's Fact-Checking Tool Can Help: **

Our Fact-Checking Tool was built for 

**Content Editors**to assist in the fact checking process and to help
reduce the likelihood that a hallucination will make its way into your
content.

Our user interface includes reference sources and
explanations-  helping users understand why their statements were
flagged as either potentially true or potentially false. These
features aim to guide users towards trusted and credible sources 

Below,  you'll find a visual of our user interface, where we used
ChatGPT-3.5 to generate a short article about a very recent news event,
and then scanned it through our tool. 

**See our Fact- Checking Tool at work: **

**Beta Users: **

We have granted 

**Beta Access**to around 40 applicants so far, and plan to continue
rolling it out on a daily basis. If you have not applied to become a
Beta User for the Fact-Checking Feature and would like to participate,
it's not too late to apply below 

*Please remember to apply with your email address associated with your
Originality.ai account* 

  

BETA USER APPLICATION 

Thanks

Cheers,

Sent to: patriogabrielpatdu@gmail.com

Unsubscribe

Jon Gillham, 1 First Street Suite #220, Collingwood, Ontario L9Y 1A1, Canada
